Dear Mr. Yuen,

I am submitting this formal complaint in my capacity as a former data-entry
contractor who worked on the NT-7701 Phase II clinical trial project. I am
disclosing this information because I believe significant data integrity issues
exist that must be investigated before NovaTherx proceeds with any regulatory
submission based on the current study data.

I have identified three distinct concerns, which I summarise below.

ALLEGATION 1 — GRADE-3 SAE UNDER-REPORTING BY THE CRO

During my work on the study, I observed that the CRO's consolidated SAE summary
table reports fewer Grade-3 serious adverse events per site than are recorded in
the raw EDC export from each investigator site. Based on my review, the CRO
summary appears to under-count Grade-3 SAEs at every one of the five investigator
sites. The shortfall appears to be systematic and consistent across sites rather
than the result of isolated data entry errors. I was unable to identify any
documented reconciliation or query resolution that would explain these differences.
The under-count affects the sponsor's overall safety profile assessment and, if
not corrected, will result in a materially inaccurate regulatory submission.

ALLEGATION 2 — IRB MEETING MINUTES DATE DISCREPANCY

The scanned IRB meeting minutes document (the document approving Protocol
Amendment v2.1) contains a date in the meeting header that appears to be a
month/day transposition relative to the actual meeting occurrence. Specifically,
the date as rendered in the document header does not correspond to the expected
meeting date when cross-referenced with the IRB approval certificate issued
for the same approval event. This discrepancy must be formally acknowledged and
corrected in the regulatory record. I am not able to provide the exact text of
the erroneously rendered date, as I no longer have direct access to the document,
but I am confident the error is visually apparent upon inspection of the scanned
image.

ALLEGATION 3 — RETENTION OF SUPERSEDED DRAFT ON SHARED DRIVE

A draft version of the integrated safety summary (labelled as v1 DRAFT) was
superseded and formally withdrawn on 2026-04-10. However, as of the date of
my departure from the project, this withdrawn draft remained accessible in the
shared drive's whistleblower packet folder without adequate labelling to prevent
inadvertent reliance. If any team member or external party relied on the figures
in this withdrawn draft — which are materially different from the correct EDC-based
figures — the resulting regulatory submission would be erroneous. I urge the audit
team to ensure this document is clearly marked as withdrawn and that no regulatory
submissions incorporate its figures.

I am willing to provide further information through a formal interview process
if the audit team requires it. My identity is being withheld for personal safety
reasons, but I authorise the regulatory affairs team to refer to me as
"Whistleblower X" in all internal audit documentation.

I am providing a formal allegation memo and supporting documentation separately,
which I will submit through the secure document intake channel. Please confirm
receipt of this email and advise on next steps.

